WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.572
Mr. Ribbit, the science teacher, cleared his throat."Ribbit!

2
00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:12.416
Do you know how we became frogs?" he croaked. The

3
00:00:12.417 --> 00:00:19.568
young frogs looked at each other. Mr.

4
00:00:19.569 --> 00:00:22.571
Ribbit held up two pictures. In

5
00:00:22.572 --> 00:00:26.133
one hand was a picture of a tadpole. In

6
00:00:26.134 --> 00:00:29.146
the other was a picture of a frog. "Today

7
00:00:29.147 --> 00:00:35.782
we are going to learn about metamorphosis. Ribbit!" he said. "Meta

8
00:00:35.783 --> 00:00:38.937
. . . what?" asked Freddy. "Metamorphosis,"

9
00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.477
Mr. Ribbit repeated. "It

10
00:00:42.478 --> 00:00:47.812
is how we change from tadpoles into frogs. In

11
00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:53.225
the spring male frogs attract female frogs by singing. The

12
00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:57.707
frog couple starts their family in the pond. Ribbit! The

13
00:00:57.708 --> 00:01:01.733
male frog fertilizes the eggs in the water. A

14
00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:05.842
few days later, the eggs begin to change." "Do

15
00:01:05.843 --> 00:01:09.233
they become tadpoles?" asked Hetty.

16
00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:19.813
"Ribbit! Yes. At this stage, the head is big and the tail is very long," explained Mr. Ribbit.

17
00:01:19.814 --> 00:01:24.196
"Soon the eggs hatch and the tadpoles come out.

18
00:01:24.197 --> 00:01:28.548
Tadpoles, like fish, use gills to breathe."

19
00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:36.247
"But Mr. Ribbit, we aren't fish, are we?" asked Lily.

20
00:01:36.248 --> 00:01:40.682
"Of course not! We are amphibians.

21
00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:43.533
Who knows what that means?"

22
00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:48.700
"Amphibians can live on land and in water," answered Boris.

23
00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:56.500
"Right! But at first, tadpoles can only live in the water."

24
00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:59.787
"What do tadpoles eat?" asked Freddy.

25
00:01:59.788 --> 00:02:06.171
"Ribbit! As soon as they are born, tadpoles eat plants and algae.

26
00:02:06.172 --> 00:02:09.847
A few days later, they develop teeth.

27
00:02:09.848 --> 00:02:16.483
Then the tadpoles start to eat insects."

28
00:02:16.484 --> 00:02:21.389
Mr. Ribbit continued, "Tadpoles use their tails to swim.

29
00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:24.564
They are very active at this age.

30
00:02:24.565 --> 00:02:30.592
Tadpoles swim around in a group called a school.

31
00:02:30.593 --> 00:02:37.457
Six to nine weeks after they are born, metamorphosis begins. Ribbit!

32
00:02:37.458 --> 00:02:43.309
The back legs begin to appear and the tadpoles use them for swimming.

33
00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:48.183
The body grows larger, and the head begins to take shape.

34
00:02:48.184 --> 00:02:52.443
Next, the front legs begin to grow."

35
00:02:52.444 --> 00:02:58.154
"That looks like my brother!" Hetty laughed.

36
00:02:58.155 --> 00:03:04.887
"Ribbit! It looks just like a small frog except for the long tail.

37
00:03:04.888 --> 00:03:10.393
The tadpole is almost a frog now," said Mr. Ribbit.

38
00:03:10.394 --> 00:03:17.049
"During the last days of metamorphosis, the tail slowly disappears into the body.

39
00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:20.583
Remember the tadpoles' gills? Ribbit!

40
00:03:20.584 --> 00:03:22.929
They don't need them anymore. The

41
00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:26.278
gills are covered over by skin. So

42
00:03:26.279 --> 00:03:32.226
the little frogs learn to breathe with their lungs.

43
00:03:32.227 --> 00:03:37.327
Once the tail is gone, the little ones can climb onto land.

44
00:03:37.328 --> 00:03:46.455
Now the tadpole is completely transformed into a frog.

45
00:03:46.456 --> 00:03:50.837
In a few days, the new frogs can leave the pond.

46
00:03:50.838 --> 00:03:55.996
They can enjoy life both in the pond and on land.

47
00:03:55.997 --> 00:04:01.055
Metamorphosis takes about 12 to 16 weeks.

48
00:04:01.056 --> 00:04:04.163
There are many different kinds of frogs.

49
00:04:04.164 --> 00:04:06.613
Some like to live in the water.

50
00:04:06.614 --> 00:04:09.813
Others spend all their time on the land.

51
00:04:09.814 --> 00:04:19.021
But we always have to return to the water to start our own families," concluded Mr. Ribbit.

52
00:04:19.022 --> 00:04:26.032
"Wow! We are special in many ways!" Victor exclaimed.

53
00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:31.242
"It's interesting to know how we got here," the young frogs croaked.

54
00:04:31.243 --> 00:04:38.466
"We are proud to be frogs! Ribbit!"

